From 18181f46786dbd64b7461cf342c0e30b2dc39bca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adidshaft <adidshaft@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:19:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Smooth brief telemetry hiccups in live HR and stress traces

The live Heart-rate and Stress traces broke into separate runs at the
strict fact-continuity gap (2 min HR / 90 s stress), so a few dropped
samples read as a jagged break instead of a continuous line.

Add a display-only continuity window
(AtriaChartVisualGrammar.traceDisplayContinuityGap = 5 min): samples
closer than this stay one shape-preserving (.monotone) run, while a real
dropout longer than five minutes still ends the run, opens a new Charts
series, and leaves the interval blank -- never bridged. The strict
data/coverage thresholds (heartRateGapThreshold, maximumFactContinuityGap)
are untouched, so telemetry-integrity and coverage accounting keep their
exact meaning.

Applies to the Vitals HR chart (smoothed + raw paths), the stress
timeline traces, and the HR-under-stress trace. Adds a regression test
pinning "3-minute hiccup connects, dropout beyond five minutes breaks".
---
 Atria/Atria/AtriaGraphGrammar.swift           | 21 ++++++++++--
 Atria/Atria/AtriaHealthScreen.swift           | 18 ++++++----
 Atria/Atria/AtriaStressDetailView.swift       | 15 ++++++--
 .../Atria/AtriaVitalsCollectionSections.swift |  9 +++--
